Z||000000||nivlek68||06-29-2000||01:13 PM||||i just bought a 86 coupe,2.5L. there is a switch in the dome light that say's preformance sound (min-max) and there is 3 plugs in the radio opening. Is the 3rd one a factory amp.If so where is it located. Did the 86 have the 4x10 in the sail panel and the speakers in the seats. Mine does just tring to see if the seats are factory. thanks in advancefor the info and sorry so long||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||06-29-2000||02:21 PM||||the performance sound system consists of the overhead switch, the wiring harness (both of witch you have), the amp which is located behind the carpet up against the right front side of the console radio pod (pull the carpet back slightly and you should see it there), and the sub-woofer itself which is located underneath the right of the dashboard (behind the dash pocket) up against the right kick panel. I have an '87GT so I am not as familiar with the '86 coupes but I do know that the speaker seats were an original factory item. most of the Fieros I have seen have 4" X 10" speakers in the dash and 4" X 6" on the pillars behind the doors......those are 3 1/2" speakers in the seats.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-29-2000||03:28 PM||||All Fieros have 4x10s in the dash.  Pre-'86s ('84s and '85s) had no sail panel speakers and 3 1/2" speakers in the headrests (seats).  '86 - '88 Fieros had no headrest speakers, but had 4x6s in the sail panels.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 07-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||nivlek68||07-03-2000||03:09 PM||||thanks for the info. sorry it took me so long to respond. behind the carpet there is a plastic panel so i didn't see the amp but found the subwoofer. i think i have to remove the console housing to get to it.<BR>who sells the adapter to hook up the factory amp to aftermarket stereo<BR>||||reg||6
